course: dictionary
lesson: 1257
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word burn is a good example. «The wood is burning in the fireplace» means on fire, with flames and heat. «I burnt the toast» means damaged by heat.
explain: Read the words around the word. «An open oven door is hot enough to burn skin instantly.» The word skin tells you burn means hurt by heat here. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Burn can be a noun too. «Cool a burn under cool running water for 20 minutes» means an injury caused by heat. Think about whether the word is doing a job like an action (a verb) or a thing (a noun).
fact: Burn is a verb: burn, burns, burned or burnt, burning.
fact: As a noun, «a burn» is an injury caused by heat, fire, chemicals or the sun.
fact: In Scotland, «a burn» is a small stream.
fact: In science, burning is a chemical change: fuel joins with oxygen and gives off heat and light, and it cannot be undone.
fact: For a burn, cool it under cool running water for 20 minutes and tell an adult.
exercise: «The wood is burning in the fireplace.» What does burning mean here? | Frozen solid | *On fire, making flames and heat | Going out and turning cold | Being carried away
exercise: «We paddled in the burn.» In Scotland, what is a burn? | A deep hole in the ground | A mark left on paper | *A small stream | A hot oven
exercise: «Cars burn petrol.» What does burn mean here? | To wash something clean | To paint something bright | To hide something away | *To use as fuel
test: «I burnt the toast.» What does burnt mean here? | Wrapped in foil | *Damaged by fire or heat | Made it wet | Ate it quickly
test: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» In science, what happens to the fuel when it burns? | It gets lighter and disappears | It is only moved to a new place | *It joins with oxygen and cannot be undone | It turns cold and hard
exam: After touching a hot pan, Sam gets a burn. What is the safest first step? | *Cool it under cool running water for 20 minutes | Wait and see if it stops hurting | Pop any blisters at once | Cover it with butter
